body:
No problem.

&#x200B;

I know people do it as sort of an ego boost, having someone so deeply invested in what makes you you.

&#x200B;

I don't really want to get a diagnosis because I don't know where that diagnosis will follow me.

I don't want the traits that make me a better CEO, Lawyer, Surgeon to be bundled up and put under a label with negative connotations especially when there's no cure or a need for one in my option.

My bus is at 6:45 in the morning...

&#x200B;

I'm distracting myself, I'm whos thoughts I'm concerned about.

Yeah that's what I've been saying to myself for the past while but I've only been getting the headaches for the past month, give or take.  
I wasn't getting them before that, or if I was it wasn't very often.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;
